{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 8750,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So today I am going to do everyone’s favorite\nnon Newtonian experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11480,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I am going to put this corn starch and water\nsolution on this speaker, but I want to do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15590,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this scientifically."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16670,
    "dDurationMs": 3171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I am shooting it with a high speed camera\nand I am going to vary the frequency and the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19841,
    "dDurationMs": 5759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "amplitude and see what factors really give\nus the best corn starch monster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25600,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It still very much looks like a liquid at\nthis point, but as I increase the amplitude,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30350,
    "dDurationMs": 5370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can kind of tell that it is not moving\nas smoothing as it should anymore."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35720,
    "dDurationMs": 14359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see at this amplitude it starts to\njump around a little bit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50079,
    "dDurationMs": 8261,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now \nI want to try to increase the frequency and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58340,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "see what effect that has."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60290,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are now at about 20 hertz, which is the\nfrequency recommended by some scientific papers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65350,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that have studied this phenomenon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66590,
    "dDurationMs": 17419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I’ll up the amplitude a little bit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84009,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is incredible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85009,
    "dDurationMs": 6441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is awesome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91450,
    "dDurationMs": 17029,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I am going up to about 22 hertz, seeing\nnicer structures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108479,
    "dDurationMs": 3021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it is really tough to tell, because it\nis somewhat random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111500,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sometimes it just turns into a blob like that\nand other times you get some really cool things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116100,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "forming."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117100,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I am about 34 hertz here and we are not seeing\na lot of structure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121320,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It seems like at these higher frequencies\nit just sort of turns into a blob."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126500,
    "dDurationMs": 6989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Interesting how it becomes more coherent and\nsmoother actually at the higher frequencies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133489,
    "dDurationMs": 3791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137280,
    "dDurationMs": 7569,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s interesting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144849,
    "dDurationMs": 10860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the high speed you can clearly see that\nthe inertia of the thing is keeping it off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155709,
    "dDurationMs": 2051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the speaker entirely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157760,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is really cool."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158760,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it is just getting kind of bumped with\nthat frequency."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162010,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is not really sticking around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163650,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That this why you probably need a lower frequency."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168630,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171230,
    "dDurationMs": 134270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, that is the end of that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305500,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how do non Newtonian fluids work?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307800,
    "dDurationMs": 3190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the corn starch and water is really\na suspension."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310990,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, these tiny little grains of starch\nsuspended in water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315050,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when you try to move that fluid slowly\nthe starch has time to get out of the way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319580,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of each other, because it is lubricated by\nall those water molecules in between."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323870,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you try to get it to go fast—and\nthat is, there is a lot of sheer, which means"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328050,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are some places that are going faster\nthan others—well, then all of the starch"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331840,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "grains kind of get stuck up against each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334120,
    "dDurationMs": 1519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they can’t flow past each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335639,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So at that point it becomes like a solid and\nless like a liquid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338889,
    "dDurationMs": 4321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, this kind of reminds me of traffic\nin LA where I have been recently."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343210,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If there are not that many cars on the road\nit is basically like having a small amount"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347180,
    "dDurationMs": 4870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of starch particles in your water and everything\nflows very smoothly, but as soon as you get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352050,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to rush hour and you have some cars which\nare trying to floor I down the highway, plus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355260,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is all of these cars, which are like\nour starch particles, on the high way, then"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359170,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "suddenly everything gets clogged and you are\nbasically in what is a solid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363210,
    "dDurationMs": 4109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So traffic might be an example of something\nthat is an non Newtonian fluid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367319,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It flows very well when there aren’t very\nmany particles or when it is going quite slowly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372009,
    "dDurationMs": 5030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as you try to increase the number of cars\nand go really fast, then everything kind of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377039,
    "dDurationMs": 671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gets clogged up."
    } ]
  } ]
}
